{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\nusing i64 = long long;\n\ni64 read() {\n    i64 x = 0;\n    char c = getchar();\n    while (c < '0' || c > '9') c = getchar();\n    while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n        x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n        c = getchar();\n    }\n    return x;\n}\n\nconst i64 MOD1 = 1000000007, MOD2 = 998244353, B = 1000000;\ni64 n, idx, ans;\nvector<i64> bucket[7];\ni64 bucketSum[7];\n\ni64 mod2(i64 x) {\n    x %= MOD2;\n    if (x < 0) x += MOD2;\n    return x;\n}\n\nvoid buildTrie(i64 cur, i64 depth) {\n    ++idx;\n    i64 val = mod2(idx - cur);\n    bucket[depth].push_back(val);\n    bucketSum[depth] = (bucketSum[depth] + val) % MOD1;\n    if (depth == 6) return;\n    for (i64 d = 0; d < 10; ++d)\n        buildTrie(cur * 10 + d, depth + 1);\n}\n\nvoid queryRange(i64 cur) {\n    if (cur > n) return;\n    \n    if (cur * B + (B - 1) <= n && cur * B * 10 > n) {\n        i64 base = idx;\n        for (i64 d = 0, mul = 1; d <= 6; ++d, mul *= 10) {\n            i64 cnt = bucket[d].size();\n            i64 offset = mod2(base - cur * mul);\n            i64 needed = (MOD2 - offset) % MOD2;\n            i64 pos = lower_bound(bucket[d].begin(), bucket[d].end(), needed) - bucket[d].begin();\n            ans = (ans + offset * cnt % MOD1 + bucketSum[d] - (cnt - pos) * MOD1) % MOD1;\n            idx += cnt;\n        }\n        return;\n    }\n    \n    ++idx;\n    ans = (ans + mod2(idx - cur)) % MOD1;\n    for (i64 d = 0; d < 10; ++d)\n        queryRange(cur * 10 + d);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    n = read();\n    buildTrie(0, 0);\n    for (i64 i = 0; i <= 6; ++i)\n        sort(bucket[i].begin(), bucket[i].end());\n    idx = 0;\n    for (i64 i = 1; i <= 9; ++i)\n        queryRange(i);\n    ans = (ans % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1;\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", ans);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD1 = 1000000007L;\n    static final long MOD2 = 998244353L;\n    static final long B = 1000000L;\n    \n    static long n, idx, ans;\n    static ArrayList<Long>[] bucket = new ArrayList[7];\n    static long[] bucketSum = new long[7];\n    \n    static long read() throws IOException {\n        long x = 0;\n        int c = System.in.read();\n        while (c < '0' || c > '9') c = System.in.read();\n        while (c >= '0' && c <= '9') {\n            x = x * 10 + (c - '0');\n            c = System.in.read();\n        }\n        return x;\n    }\n    \n    static long mod2(long x) {\n        x %= MOD2;\n        if (x < 0) x += MOD2;\n        return x;\n    }\n    \n    static void buildTrie(long cur, int depth) {\n        ++idx;\n        long val = mod2(idx - cur);\n        bucket[depth].add(val);\n        bucketSum[depth] = (bucketSum[depth] + val) % MOD1;\n        if (depth == 6) return;\n        for (long d = 0; d < 10; ++d) {\n            buildTrie(cur * 10 + d, depth + 1);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static void queryRange(long cur) {\n        if (cur > n) return;\n        \n        if (cur * B + (B - 1) <= n && cur * B * 10 > n) {\n            long base = idx;\n            for (int d = 0, mul = 1; d <= 6; ++d, mul *= 10) {\n                long cnt = bucket[d].size();\n                long offset = mod2(base - cur * mul);\n                long needed = (MOD2 - offset) % MOD2;\n                long pos = lowerBound(bucket[d], needed);\n                long term1 = offset * cnt % MOD1;\n                long term2 = bucketSum[d];\n                long term3 = (cnt - pos) * MOD1 % MOD1;\n                ans = (ans + term1 + term2 - term3) % MOD1;\n                idx += cnt;\n            }\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        ++idx;\n        ans = (ans + mod2(idx - cur)) % MOD1;\n        for (long d = 0; d < 10; ++d) {\n            queryRange(cur * 10 + d);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static long lowerBound(ArrayList<Long> list, long key) {\n        int low = 0, high = list.size();\n        while (low < high) {\n            int mid = (low + high) >>> 1;\n            if (list.get(mid) < key) {\n                low = mid + 1;\n            } else {\n                high = mid;\n            }\n        }\n        return low;\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        for (int i = 0; i < 7; ++i) {\n            bucket[i] = new ArrayList<>();\n        }\n        n = read();\n        idx = 0;\n        buildTrie(0, 0);\n        for (int i = 0; i <= 6; ++i) {\n            Collections.sort(bucket[i]);\n        }\n        idx = 0;\n        ans = 0;\n        for (long i = 1; i <= 9; ++i) {\n            queryRange(i);\n        }\n        ans = (ans % MOD1 + MOD1) % MOD1;\n        System.out.println(ans);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00023862851958256215, -2.622600959512056e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -4.9232225137529895e-05, -2.0265373677830212e-05, -0.42